  step,dige:573d64e5e69a8860
  step=2,desc:stand a host that time comes in by — Clock_A hears its beat — K_P and K_Q hear the clock — the outside says 1000 ms and runs,dige:ea43a1b0ddd1aaee
    Assertion:time-comes-in-only,sentence:time comes in only through the host — what the outside said is on its tape and a beat reaches the tanks two rounds later
  step=3,desc:the timer runs early then late — the outside says 400 and 900 and runs — then 2300 and runs,dige:c517b2df0615002c
    Assertion:the-host-turns-the,sentence:the host turns the outside’s ms into whole beats — what is left over waits as spare so an early or late timer loses nothing
  step=4,desc:keep the tape — stand the pond again from nothing — play the tape into the new host,dige:efb43be9d3db1640
    Assertion:replaying-the-tape-runs,sentence:replaying the tape runs as the outside ran — run for run and round for round
    Assertion:the-replayed-tanks-end,sentence:the replayed tanks end as the live ones did — every egg and fish and turn
    Assertion:a-replay-hears-exactly,sentence:a replay hears exactly the tape it played — the tape is the whole outside
